# STAGE skill roots

Cursor discovers both `.cursor/skills/` and the tool-neutral shared root `.agents/skills/`, and may also ingest compatibility roots. All carry the same sixteen `stage-*` skills, but only the Cursor copy names Cursor's tools.

| Root | Harness wording |
|---|---|
| `.agents/skills/` | tool-neutral shared root; bare skill names and role-based capability wording |
| `.claude/skills/` | Claude Code: `/stage-*`, `Bash`, `Read`, `AskUserQuestion`, `Agent` |
| `.cursor/skills/` | Cursor: `/stage-*`, `Shell`, `Read`, `AskQuestion`, `Task` |
| `.dsh/skills/` | DSH: `/skill:stage-*`, `bash`, `read`, `ask_user_question`, `subagent` |
| `.kimi-code/skills/` | Kimi Code: `/skill:stage-*`, `Bash`, `Read`, `AskUserQuestion`, `Agent` |
| `.pi/skills/` | Pi: `/stage-*`, lower-case built-ins plus STAGE's prefixed extensions |
| `.qwen/skills/` | Qwen Code: `/stage-*`, `run_shell_command`, `read_file`, `ask_user_question`, `agent` |

When duplicate names are surfaced, load and follow `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`; the path shown by discovery does not change ownership. The shared root remains a safe fallback because it names no other harness's tools, but Cursor-native wording is preferred when present.

The six decision-point skills — `stage-proj-adopt`, `stage-stry-coach`, `stage-outl-planner`, `stage-resp-writer`, `stage-subm-packer`, and `stage-pstr-builder` — remain slash-only and must not be started without the user's explicit choice.
